  "120347": {
   "citation": "(120347) Salacia = 2004 SB60<br><br>Salacia is the Roman goddess of the calm and sunlit ocean.  At first afraid of Neptune's advances, she was convinced to agree to marriage by the dolphin Delphinus. </pre> The following citation is from <i>MPC</i> 73984: <p><pre> S/(120347) 1 Actaea = S/2006 (120347) 1 <br><br>Actaea is one of the Nereids.  She is portrayed as a nymph of the shore. The Nereids were among the attendants of Salacia. ",
