  "90482": {
   "citation": "(90482) Orcus I = Vanth<br><br>Vanth is a daimon in Etruscan mythology who guides the dead to the underworld.  She often appears on tomb paintings and sarcophagi, where she is depicted with wings and a torch.  She is frequently shown in the presence of Charun, a guard of the underworld.  The name was suggested by S. Taaffe. ",
